00:27:35,176 --> 00:27:37,549
I just felt sorry for you.

260
00:27:37,549 --> 00:27:42,249
I did nothing wrong,
but I put up with it out of sympathy.

261
00:27:42,963 --> 00:27:45,016
And this is how you behave?

262
00:27:49,052 --> 00:27:50,904
I am

263
00:27:50,904 --> 00:27:52,983
just as

264
00:27:52,983 --> 00:27:55,160
uncomfortable as you are.

265
00:27:55,160 --> 00:27:57,232
You're not the only one who's uncomfortable,

266
00:27:57,232 --> 00:27:59,149
so don't make such a big deal out of it.

267
00:28:00,044 --> 00:28:02,316
From now on, I'm not treating you
like my senior anymore.

268
00:28:02,316 --> 00:28:05,683
You brought this on yourself,
so you deal with it.

269
00:28:06,928 --> 00:28:08,628
Understood?

270
00:28:13,760 --> 00:28:15,460
Go back to work.

271
00:28:30,600 --> 00:28:34,316
Of all days, this happens on my first
half-day off since becoming team leader.

272
00:28:35,496 --> 00:28:37,664
You both need to get your heads on straight.

273
00:28:37,664 --> 00:28:41,136
You're supposed to be learning the job,
so don't get caught up in this nonsense.

274
00:28:41,136 --> 00:28:42,836
You're not children.

275
00:28:43,649 --> 00:28:45,992
- Yes.
- I'm sorry.

276
00:28:45,992 --> 00:28:47,692
I'm sorry.

277
00:29:07,296 --> 00:29:08,996
Come in.

278
00:29:15,116 --> 00:29:17,783
Here's last week's sales report.

279
00:29:18,508 --> 00:29:20,960
And the report on the new business.

280
00:29:20,960 --> 00:29:23,716
At this rate, I'm going to
get buried alive under paperwork.

281
00:29:23,716 --> 00:29:25,030
And I made this into a graph

282
00:29:25,030 --> 00:29:28,583
showing changes in consumer patterns
year over year.

283
00:29:28,583 --> 00:29:33,092
And here's the regional breakdown
of the overseas brand sales you asked for.

284
00:29:33,092 --> 00:29:35,716
Do you know what your problem is?

285
00:29:35,716 --> 00:29:38,020
There are so many that I don't even know
what you're referring to.

286
00:29:38,020 --> 00:29:40,264
You don't give me a rhythm.

287
00:29:40,264 --> 00:29:42,764
You should give me
the work little by little too.

288
00:29:42,764 --> 00:29:45,552
Oh, I didn't think of that.

289
00:29:45,552 --> 00:29:48,764
You do the same thing with your team.

290
00:29:48,764 --> 00:29:50,492
I hear Team 5 is a mess.

291
00:29:50,492 --> 00:29:53,000
Yeah, I saw a new side of Team Leader Gong.

292
00:29:53,000 --> 00:29:54,516
He's got quite a temper.

293
00:29:54,516 --> 00:29:56,312
Well, he probably learned it all from you.

294
00:29:56,312 --> 00:29:58,896
I learned it from you, Department Head.

295
00:29:58,896 --> 00:30:01,249
How's Laknes? Think he'll do well?

296
00:30:01,249 --> 00:30:04,224
You know Team Leader Gong.
He's better than average.

297
00:30:04,224 --> 00:30:06,516
He understands the bigger picture too.

298
00:30:07,892 --> 00:30:11,412
People who see the big picture
can also make big mistakes.

299
00:30:11,412 --> 00:30:12,516
Keep a close eye on him.

300
00:30:12,516 --> 00:30:13,516
Yes, ma'am.

301
00:30:13,516 --> 00:30:15,549
And get Assistant Manager Yang's situation
sorted out too.

302
00:30:15,549 --> 00:30:17,736
Things that are going to blow up
will blow up.

303
00:30:17,736 --> 00:30:20,516
But we can't leave the mess
sitting there once it does.

304
00:30:21,132 --> 00:30:22,224
Yes, understood, ma'am.

305
00:30:22,224 --> 00:30:23,924
Well, then...

306
00:30:29,752 --> 00:30:34,116
I'm telling you, rhythm is important,
Deputy Director Jang.

307
00:30:39,252 --> 00:30:40,952
Let's see.

308
00:30:44,883 --> 00:30:45,883
Joo Hee?

309
00:30:45,883 --> 00:30:47,252
Oh, ma'am.

310
00:30:47,252 --> 00:30:48,252
What are you looking for?

311
00:30:48,252 --> 00:30:50,532
I'm trying to find last year's catalog.

312
00:30:50,532 --> 00:30:51,916
Why do you need last year's catalog?

313
00:30:51,916 --> 00:30:55,312
Oh, the Osiris designs
this year look familiar.

314
00:30:55,312 --> 00:30:57,383
So I want to look into it.

315
00:30:59,924 --> 00:31:03,180
Let me ask you something.

316
00:31:03,180 --> 00:31:07,680
Is your team getting any brands
from another team?

317
00:31:07,680 --> 00:31:09,020
Like what?

318
00:31:09,020 --> 00:31:10,812
I mean,

319
00:31:10,812 --> 00:31:15,556
are you getting anything
from Team 4 or Team 5?

320
00:31:15,556 --> 00:31:17,724
Oh.

321
00:31:17,724 --> 00:31:21,080
I'm not really sure about that.

322
00:31:21,080 --> 00:31:23,983
Oh, really?

323
00:31:23,983 --> 00:31:25,883
Should I find out?

324
00:31:25,883 --> 00:31:28,688
No, forget it.

325
00:31:28,688 --> 00:31:33,520
Just let me know if you hear anything.

326
00:31:33,520 --> 00:31:35,783
Yes, ma'am.

327
00:31:35,783 --> 00:31:36,783
Keep up the good work.

328
00:31:36,783 --> 00:31:38,483
Thanks.

329
00:32:04,548 --> 00:32:06,949
Yes, sir. I'm on the phone.

330
00:32:08,336 --> 00:32:10,036
Pardon?

331
00:32:16,748 --> 00:32:18,316
See? I knew it.

332
00:32:18,316 --> 00:32:20,883
I knew I'd find you here.

333
00:32:23,532 --> 00:32:25,684
Everyone probably knows I'm here.

334
00:32:25,684 --> 00:32:27,980
That's why no one else comes up.

335
00:32:27,980 --> 00:32:29,352
I'm okay to come up, right?

336
00:32:29,352 --> 00:32:32,448
I was your first mentor here, remember?

337
00:32:32,448 --> 00:32:35,349
I started off on the wrong foot.

338
00:32:36,864 --> 00:32:39,240
The guy who got chewed out is working hard.

339
00:32:39,240 --> 00:32:42,260
And the one who did the chewing out
is all torn up about it. Oh, boy.

340
00:32:42,260 --> 00:32:45,028
So what got into you all of a sudden?

341
00:32:45,028 --> 00:32:47,464
It was something I had to do sooner or later.

342
00:32:47,464 --> 00:32:50,649
Just this once?
You should've done it dozens of times.

343
00:32:52,412 --> 00:32:53,948
So you think I did the right thing?

344
00:32:53,948 --> 00:32:55,449
No.

345
00:32:55,449 --> 00:32:58,372
Either you push back again and again,
or you put up with it to the end.

346
00:32:58,372 --> 00:33:00,716
You should've picked one.

347
00:33:00,716 --> 00:33:01,716
Jeez.

348
00:33:01,716 --> 00:33:04,716
It's driving you crazy having to
go downstairs and face them, isn't it?

349
00:33:05,649 --> 00:33:07,312
Mr. Jung,

350
00:33:07,312 --> 00:33:09,360
back when we were
on Deputy Director Jang's team,

351
00:33:09,360 --> 00:33:11,644
he used to chew me out all the time.

352
00:33:11,644 --> 00:33:13,008
I know.

353
00:33:13,008 --> 00:33:14,816
I'll tell you this now.

354
00:33:14,816 --> 00:33:16,996
Back then, we even had bets
on when you'd quit.

355
00:33:16,996 --> 00:33:19,992
You know what was really ridiculous
about him back then?

356
00:33:19,992 --> 00:33:21,164
You bet on it?

357
00:33:21,164 --> 00:33:24,404
Yeah. Go on. Tell me.

358
00:33:24,404 --> 00:33:27,092
Anyway, the really ridiculous part was

359
00:33:27,092 --> 00:33:29,640
he'd chew me out like he wanted to kill me,

360
00:33:29,640 --> 00:33:32,524
but then he acted like nothing happened
and even put his arm around me.

361
00:33:32,524 --> 00:33:34,508
I know. I went through plenty of it too.

362
00:33:34,508 --> 00:33:37,583
So I was convinced he was
either a psychopath or a sociopath

363
00:33:37,583 --> 00:33:39,383
or some kind of "-path."

364
00:33:39,383 --> 00:33:41,683
I still think so.
He's definitely some kind of "-path."

365
00:33:41,683 --> 00:33:46,016
But now that I'm in the same situation,

366
00:33:46,016 --> 00:33:50,949
I'm wondering if I should go downstairs
and pretend we're friends.

367
00:33:51,572 --> 00:33:54,848
Back then,
when Deputy Director Jang did that,

368
00:33:54,848 --> 00:33:57,296
I just took it as him
wanting to bury the hatchet.

369
00:33:57,296 --> 00:33:59,983
Why? Is there anything else
to it in a company?

370
00:33:59,983 --> 00:34:02,532
You just let things go and move on.

371
00:34:02,532 --> 00:34:04,680
I'm sure Yang Jun Ho will do the same.

372
00:34:04,680 --> 00:34:07,868
Then should I do
what Deputy Director Jang did too?

373
00:34:07,868 --> 00:34:10,016
Then you'll become a psychopath too.

374
00:34:10,016 --> 00:34:11,840
- Oh, boy.
- No, oh, jeez.

375
00:34:11,840 --> 00:34:13,660
Well, oh...

376
00:34:13,660 --> 00:34:15,604
Sir, how long have you been there?

377
00:34:15,604 --> 00:34:19,783
You punks are just sitting around
badmouthing your boss during work hours.

378
00:34:20,904 --> 00:34:23,316
You, come with me. We've got somewhere to go.

379
00:34:24,672 --> 00:34:25,783
I'll deal with you tomorrow.

380
00:34:25,783 --> 00:34:28,220
No, that's not what we meant, Mr. Jang!

381
00:34:28,220 --> 00:34:30,556
Put in a good word for me.

382
00:34:30,556 --> 00:34:33,049
You were the one who brought up
the psychopath thing.

383
00:34:55,148 --> 00:34:59,300
Put half as much sincerity into me
as you do into beef.

384
00:34:59,300 --> 00:35:01,383
Then I'll carry you around on my back.

385
00:35:03,328 --> 00:35:05,648
You're paying for this today.

386
00:35:05,648 --> 00:35:08,472
It's an unwritten rule that
if you get caught badmouthing your boss,

387
00:35:08,472 --> 00:35:10,400
you buy beef.

388
00:35:10,400 --> 00:35:12,416
I was actually planning to pay today.

389
00:35:12,416 --> 00:35:14,588
Look at you.

390
00:35:14,588 --> 00:35:17,216
No excuses, no denial.

391
00:35:17,216 --> 00:35:18,800
Just full of confidence, huh?

392
00:35:18,800 --> 00:35:20,749
Thank you.

393
00:35:22,988 --> 00:35:28,832
So, have you narrowed down
the brands to transfer to Team 1?

394
00:35:28,832 --> 00:35:30,580
Yes, about that.

395
00:35:30,580 --> 00:35:32,476
They're definitely going to Team 1, right?

396
00:35:32,476 --> 00:35:35,264
Why are you asking when you already know?

397
00:35:35,264 --> 00:35:37,749
Let's get Team Leader Kim promoted.

398
00:35:38,560 --> 00:35:41,096
I'll sort them out and hand them over
by the end of the week.

399
00:35:41,096 --> 00:35:44,828
What's there to think about?
Just give them all the questionable ones.

400
00:35:44,828 --> 00:35:48,049
They may look questionable to others,

401
00:35:48,049 --> 00:35:50,040
but aren't they like my children?

402
00:35:50,040 --> 00:35:53,332
That's why I let you adopt a kid
who can get into SNU all on their own.

403
00:35:53,332 --> 00:35:55,116
I mean, Laknes.

404
00:35:55,992 --> 00:35:58,149
Oh, man.

405
00:36:02,812 --> 00:36:06,416
Well, if I may ask a bold question,

406
00:36:06,416 --> 00:36:10,649
was Team Leader Jung completely
excluded from consideration for promotion?

407
00:36:12,400 --> 00:36:15,849
He's the one choosing not to go for it.
It's not like I'm holding him back.

408
00:36:27,968 --> 00:36:30,316
Yeah, here!

409
00:36:30,953 --> 00:36:32,820
I told him to come here.

410
00:36:32,820 --> 00:36:36,249
It's not like he's your mortal enemy.
What's the big deal?

411
00:36:37,716 --> 00:36:40,796
Wait, you're leaving?

412
00:36:40,796 --> 00:36:44,680
I'll pay for this. Finish your meal.

413
00:36:44,680 --> 00:36:47,636
Oh, and when I said to let things go
with Team Leader Jung,

414
00:36:47,636 --> 00:36:51,783
I wasn't trying to bury the hatchet
while it's still raw.

415
00:36:51,783 --> 00:36:54,049
I was trying to say,
let's just get it off our chest.

416
00:36:55,508 --> 00:36:58,576
What are you doing? Go sit down, you punk.

417
00:36:58,576 --> 00:37:00,276
What?

418
00:37:14,984 --> 00:37:18,884
Today was actually a day
when I really wanted some beef.

419
00:37:18,884 --> 00:37:23,440
And I ended up eating it with you,
Assistant Manager Yang.

420
00:37:23,440 --> 00:37:26,412
Why are you suddenly speaking formally again?

421
00:37:26,412 --> 00:37:29,216
Of course, I'm going to keep
speaking formally.

422
00:37:31,292 --> 00:37:33,683
Why are we taking this so far?

423
00:37:36,449 --> 00:37:38,532
I think we definitely need a drink for this.

424
00:37:38,532 --> 00:37:40,349
Yeah, I think so too.

425
00:37:46,680 --> 00:37:48,796
Assistant Manager Yang,

426
00:37:48,796 --> 00:37:51,216
can I ask you something?

427
00:37:51,216 --> 00:37:53,249
Speak your mind.

428
00:37:54,352 --> 00:37:58,983
Is someone like me
that important in your life?

429
00:38:01,516 --> 00:38:05,492
I don't really know what you mean.

430
00:38:05,492 --> 00:38:07,616
Well,

431
00:38:07,616 --> 00:38:11,216
something very significant
happened to me over the weekend.

432
00:38:11,216 --> 00:38:13,249
Something that made me...

433
00:38:15,649 --> 00:38:18,049
rethink my entire life.

434
00:38:19,616 --> 00:38:22,116
But after thinking about it all weekend,

435
00:38:23,408 --> 00:38:26,816
I realized the biggest obstacle
in my life right now...

436
00:38:29,264 --> 00:38:31,283
was you, Assistant Manager Yang.

437
00:38:35,580 --> 00:38:40,428
So I thought about whether that meant
you were really that important in my life.

438
00:38:40,428 --> 00:38:42,480
But I realized you weren't.

439
00:38:42,480 --> 00:38:44,376
And I think it's the same for you.

440
00:38:44,376 --> 00:38:49,656
Haven't we just been living different lives
for 30 years before we met?

441
00:38:49,656 --> 00:38:52,283
If we get along, it's a blessing,

442
00:38:52,283 --> 00:38:56,116
but it's not something to be anxious
or frustrated about if we don't.

443
00:38:56,116 --> 00:38:57,556
Yeah, I suppose you're right.

444
00:38:57,556 --> 00:39:01,516
Right, we're not important to each other.

445
00:39:02,720 --> 00:39:05,083
So there's no need for us to fight like this.

446
00:39:07,508 --> 00:39:09,983
Let me ask you something, then.

447
00:39:12,296 --> 00:39:17,049
Why did you treat me like that all this time?

448
00:39:21,905 --> 00:39:24,516
- Let's have another drink.
- Yeah, sure.

449
00:39:39,452 --> 00:39:43,249
Do you think you're the victim here?

450
00:39:45,983 --> 00:39:49,268
What do you think a team member is?

451
00:39:49,268 --> 00:39:54,480
I mean, when you make an important decision,

452
00:39:54,480 --> 00:39:57,583
have you ever asked for our input?

453
00:39:58,284 --> 00:40:00,500
In all the time I've worked here,

454
00:40:00,500 --> 00:40:03,168
I've never felt like
I was an important member

455
00:40:03,168 --> 00:40:07,483
of the team working alongside you.

456
00:40:08,632 --> 00:40:10,612
Think about it, Mr. Gong.

457
00:40:10,612 --> 00:40:14,683
<i>I wasn't like this with you
from the beginning.</i>

458
00:40:19,228 --> 00:40:22,704
I made a promise to myself
when I started working with you.

459
00:40:22,704 --> 00:40:24,840
"Don't expect to be treated like a senior."

460
00:40:24,840 --> 00:40:28,180
"Just do my best as a team member."

461
00:40:28,180 --> 00:40:30,349
But you...

462
00:40:31,368 --> 00:40:32,806
Forget about treating me like a senior.

463
00:40:32,806 --> 00:40:34,883
You don't even treat me like a team member.

464
00:40:34,883 --> 00:40:37,408
You never ask what we're thinking

465
00:40:37,408 --> 00:40:41,324
or whether we're having
any difficulties at work.

466
00:40:41,324 --> 00:40:46,180
You only care whether things are getting done
according to your standards.

467
00:40:46,180 --> 00:40:48,283
Isn't this a company?

468
00:40:48,283 --> 00:40:49,904
We're people who met to work, aren't we?

469
00:40:49,904 --> 00:40:53,516
Yes. That's what you think.

470
00:40:55,836 --> 00:40:58,316
Maybe you don't see it that way,

471
00:40:58,316 --> 00:41:01,749
but you are important to me, Mr. Gong.

472
00:41:07,248 --> 00:41:08,823
As you know, people in my group

473
00:41:08,823 --> 00:41:10,449
weren't hired
through the regular recruitment process.

474
00:41:10,449 --> 00:41:11,483
[Hongsung International
Personnel Appointment Notice]

475
00:41:11,483 --> 00:41:12,536
[Assistant Manager Gong Promoted to Manager]
<i>So my years of service</i>

476
00:41:12,536 --> 00:41:14,649
<i>weren't fully recognized, either.</i>

477
00:41:15,756 --> 00:41:17,212
[Assistant Manager Gong Promoted to Manager]
<i>Do you really think</i>

478
00:41:17,212 --> 00:41:20,932
<i>that's the only reason
you were promoted before me?</i>

479
00:41:20,932 --> 00:41:23,249
<i>Are you saying there was another reason?</i>

480
00:41:23,249 --> 00:41:24,676
<i>Yes.</i>

481
00:41:24,676 --> 00:41:27,483
Because you are better than me.

482
00:41:28,384 --> 00:41:30,700
Regardless of seniority,

483
00:41:30,700 --> 00:41:34,000
if I were better,
I would've been promoted first, right?

484
00:41:34,000 --> 00:41:36,249
That's how companies work.

485
00:41:39,092 --> 00:41:42,160
But I just wanted to get in your way somehow.

486
00:41:42,160 --> 00:41:46,149
You're younger than me,
yet you seem better than me.

487
00:41:48,576 --> 00:41:51,449
Saying it out loud
makes me feel like a real idiot.

488
00:41:57,000 --> 00:41:58,716
No, I also...

489
00:41:59,816 --> 00:42:03,224
I thought I understood
what you were going through,

490
00:42:03,224 --> 00:42:04,752
but I was wrong.

491
00:42:04,752 --> 00:42:07,116
I'm sorry too.

492
00:42:07,116 --> 00:42:09,684
Anyway, I'm sorry.

493
00:42:09,684 --> 00:42:13,484
In the end, all this happened
because of my own shortcomings.

494
00:42:13,484 --> 00:42:16,716
No. Hearing you say that,
I realize I wasn't blameless, either.

495
00:42:19,416 --> 00:42:22,408
I'll submit my resignation letter
by tomorrow.

496
00:42:22,408 --> 00:42:25,680
Well, I'll make sure everything
is properly handed over before I leave,

497
00:42:25,680 --> 00:42:27,449
so don't worry.

498
00:42:27,449 --> 00:42:29,672
<i>Oh, and when I said to let things go
with Team Leader Jung,</i>

499
00:42:29,672 --> 00:42:33,024
I wasn't trying to bury the hatchet
while it's still raw.

500
00:42:33,024 --> 00:42:35,216
<i>I was trying to say,
let's just get it off our chest.</i>

501
00:42:38,996 --> 00:42:41,516
Do you really have to do this?

502
00:42:43,988 --> 00:42:46,816
I just can't deal with going to work anymore.

503
00:42:46,816 --> 00:42:50,456
I'm the kind of guy who gets pushed around
by a younger team leader

504
00:42:50,456 --> 00:42:53,216
and gets cursed at, right?

505
00:42:53,216 --> 00:42:56,883
Then by that logic, I'm a team leader
who can't even manage one team member

506
00:42:56,883 --> 00:42:59,949
and just humiliates him in front of everyone.

507
00:43:02,420 --> 00:43:04,528
Actually...

508
00:43:04,528 --> 00:43:08,083
I was seriously thinking about quitting too.

509
00:43:09,264 --> 00:43:13,049
But if we both quit now,

510
00:43:13,892 --> 00:43:16,844
wouldn't that mean we both quit
because we lost to each other?

511
00:43:16,844 --> 00:43:18,949
Let's not do that.

512
00:43:21,020 --> 00:43:22,720
Assistant Manager Yang,

513
00:43:23,372 --> 00:43:25,256
well...

514
00:43:25,256 --> 00:43:28,572
Putting aside the fact
that we don't get along personally,

515
00:43:28,572 --> 00:43:31,516
what do you think of me professionally?

516
00:43:34,464 --> 00:43:36,276
<i>There have been times.</i>

517
00:43:36,276 --> 00:43:40,244
<i>"God, I really can't stand him,
but he's good at his job."</i>

518
00:43:40,244 --> 00:43:43,652
<i>All the brands we brought in
were practically doomed, weren't they?</i>

519
00:43:43,652 --> 00:43:46,036
<i>I'll give you that.</i>

520
00:43:46,036 --> 00:43:49,683
<i>You're really good at seeing the big picture
and driving things forward.</i>

521
00:43:50,680 --> 00:43:52,880
I felt the same way.

522
00:43:52,880 --> 00:43:56,224
I'd think, "I really don't
get along with this guy,"

523
00:43:56,224 --> 00:43:58,216
<i>"but he's really good at his job."</i>

524
00:43:58,216 --> 00:44:00,749
<i>"He didn't get this far for nothing."</i>

525
00:44:00,749 --> 00:44:04,516
<i>Your attention to the details
that others overlook is impressive.</i>

526
00:44:08,092 --> 00:44:09,792
Is that so?

527
00:44:17,836 --> 00:44:19,949
So, Assistant Manager Yang, I was thinking,

528
00:44:21,384 --> 00:44:23,283
let's just work together.

529
00:44:24,128 --> 00:44:25,649
Work?

530
00:44:25,649 --> 00:44:27,383
Assistant Manager Yang,

531
00:44:28,016 --> 00:44:30,383
would you like to stir up
some trouble with me?

532
00:44:31,916 --> 00:44:35,516
Whoa, why are you making me nervous?

533
00:44:38,249 --> 00:44:40,716
I'm going to shake things up at the company.

534
00:45:01,030 --> 00:45:05,012
[Gangnam]

535
00:45:05,012 --> 00:45:06,249
Yes, sir.

536
00:45:06,249 --> 00:45:10,332
So while you're at it,
you should register as a rental business

537
00:45:10,332 --> 00:45:13,449
and learn how to issue
electronic tax invoices.

538
00:45:13,449 --> 00:45:17,549
That's how people end up going
from tax avoidance to tax evasion.

539
00:45:17,549 --> 00:45:21,583
Yes, yes. Go ahead.

540
00:45:22,392 --> 00:45:24,316
Oh, sorry about that.

541
00:45:24,316 --> 00:45:25,316
My call ran long.

542
00:45:25,316 --> 00:45:27,060
Not at all. It's fine.

543
00:45:27,060 --> 00:45:30,452
So you're looking at
both commercial properties and apartments?

544
00:45:30,452 --> 00:45:32,044
I haven't decided yet.

545
00:45:32,044 --> 00:45:36,616
But I'm mainly looking for places
that can generate stable rental income.

546
00:45:36,616 --> 00:45:39,849
Do you have enough capital?
Would you need a loan?

547
00:45:39,849 --> 00:45:41,600
I do have some thoughts about it.

548
00:45:41,600 --> 00:45:44,816
But I'd prefer to do it without a loan.

549
00:45:44,816 --> 00:45:47,456
You must be doing quite well
for someone so young.

550
00:45:47,456 --> 00:45:49,460
- Are you a salaried employee?
- Yes.

551
00:45:49,460 --> 00:45:51,312
Oh, you've made a good decision.

552
00:45:51,312 --> 00:45:55,336
These days, you can't get very far
on earned income alone.

553
00:45:55,336 --> 00:45:59,516
If you can afford it, you need something
like a building to fall back on.

554
00:46:00,780 --> 00:46:04,892
Excuse me for asking,
but what is your annual salary?

555
00:46:04,892 --> 00:46:07,288
Well, it's around 70 million won.

556
00:46:07,288 --> 00:46:08,788
But does that really matter?

557
00:46:08,788 --> 00:46:11,148
Of course, it does. It's very important.

558
00:46:11,148 --> 00:46:14,732
It means you're worth over three billion won.

559
00:46:14,732 --> 00:46:19,480
To make 70 million won a year
in rent after taxes and expenses,

560
00:46:19,480 --> 00:46:21,956
the building would have to be worth
over three billion won.

561
00:46:21,956 --> 00:46:26,916
So someone earning that much a year
is effectively worth three billion won.

562
00:46:26,916 --> 00:46:28,949
Well, what a valuable client we've got here.

563
00:46:30,252 --> 00:46:31,608
I guess so.

564
00:46:31,608 --> 00:46:33,449
When you put it that way,

565
00:46:34,216 --> 00:46:35,904
I guess I'm worth three billion won.

566
00:46:35,904 --> 00:46:38,920
A lot of people
buy lottery tickets these days, right?

567
00:46:38,920 --> 00:46:43,216
That's because
they don't know their own worth.

568
00:46:43,216 --> 00:46:46,356
Alright, let's see.

569
00:46:46,356 --> 00:46:48,920
For apartments, this neighborhood is good.

570
00:46:48,920 --> 00:46:49,936
As for buildings,

571
00:46:49,936 --> 00:46:51,564
- there are so many variables...
- I'm sorry.

572
00:46:51,564 --> 00:46:55,380
- But I'll come back another time.
- Pardon?

573
00:46:55,380 --> 00:46:56,722
Like you said,

574
00:46:56,722 --> 00:47:00,464
something worth three billion
shouldn't be controlled by 1.3 billion.

575
00:47:00,464 --> 00:47:02,649
What is the 1.3 billion about?

